omestic lives with  her children she wishes to travel into  one of these other dimensions so that  she can take another wonders place and  raise her kids in peace such an action  could lead to dire consequences but  wonder doesn't care she just wants her  children back to accomplish her goal  wonder tracks america through the  multiverse so that she can train her of  her powers to use them for her own gain  such a process will kill america but  wonder doesn't care she's made a major  heel turn from the last time we've seen  her and it all appears to be a result of  the darkhold corrupting her after all  it's not like wanda's always been this  way one could look at her character  rocking captain america civil war as  evidence of this in that film she  accidentally kills some people during  her attempt to stop some bad guys and  she feels terrible about it in that  instance she obviously knows the ends  don't justify the means and it  kickstarts the entire conflict of the  film suffice to say that's not how she  acts in this movie but her turn to  villainy will come as no surprise to  people who know the comics scarlet witch  it was fun just looking at it from a  different perspective  wanda started as a villain in the mcu  only to turn into an avenger and now in  doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness she's back to being the bad guy  and she does some truly horrific things  from slaughtering sorcerers at carmitage  to killing the illuminati she doesn't  allow anyone to get in her path to  capturing america it can naturally make  the audience conflicted about how to  feel about her and that's precisely the  case with her status in the marvel  comics she's done plenty of good  throughout her comic book run helping  the avengers and the x-men numerous  times however she's also caused her fair  share of problems particularly when she  becomes overly emotional this is  precisely what occurred during the  infamous house of m storyline where she  created an alternate 